@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il27-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il27-tax-years`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Retirement Age Law, 5764-2004 (חוק גיל פרישה). Row IL-27. Source: ../../../retirement-age-law-5764-2004/registers/source-bundle/retirement-age-law-5764-2004.he.wiki.txt
-- (sha256 633aa70f0cd151e65bccc91c1341e0784a13d93311d79b65e5a4ecedb1dfa1bd), Hebrew Wikisource, an unofficial consolidation; the file tag is `ral`.
--
-- WHY THIS LAW. Income Tax Ordinance s 1 defines "retirement age" (גיל הפרישה) as "retirement age as meant in the Retirement Age Law" (ITO line 115), and
-- s 37 (credit for a spouse), s 9(16A) and others turn on an individual or his spouse having "reached the retirement age". Rows IL-08 and IL-07 took
-- that as an input (fork F20 of row IL-08). The Law has 34 sections, not 37: the "section 37" of this row's brief is ITO s 37.
--
-- WHAT IS ENCODED: the retirement age. s 3: 67 for a man, 65 for a woman. s 6: for a man born up to April 1942 the age the Schedule's Part A fixes by birth month;
-- for a woman born up to December 1969 the age Part B fixes by birth month. The ages are in years and months, held here in months.
-- Not encoded, each with its reason (NOTES.md): s 4 (the compulsory retirement age, 67) and s 5 and Part C (the early retirement age) and ss 7 and 8 (their
-- transitional rules), because no section of the Ordinance in scope turns on them; s 10 (the Law prevails over agreements, with exceptions) and s 12 (an age agreed
-- before the Law for a woman applies "for her entitlement to retire and to receive a benefit from her employer, and for that purpose only"), which do not change
-- "the retirement age" the Ordinance means; ss 11 and 13 to 31 (notices, state aid, indirect amendments) and 32 to 34.
--
-- GAP. Part B, as deposited, has no row for a woman born before May 1947 (its first row is "מאי 1947 עד דצמבר 1959"; the Wikisource table has no header row, and Part C,
-- for the early retirement age, does have a row "עד אפריל 1947"). The rule refuses by name for such a woman: "needs a source" (the Knesset text, Sefer HaChukim 5764 p. 150).
-- ===========================================================================

§ `The Retirement Age Law — the retirement age`

-- ext:[ral:42] | הגיל שבהגיעו אליו זכאי אדם לפרוש מעבודתו בשל גילו ולקבל, בהתקיים התנאים הקבועים לכך על פי דין או הסכם, גמלה בשל פרישתו מעבודתו כאמור, הוא גיל 67 לגבר וגיל 65 לאישה (בחוק זה – גיל הפרישה).
-- ext:[ral:53] | על אף האמור בסעיף 3 –
-- ext:[ral:54] | (1) לגבי גבר שנולד עד חודש אפריל 1942, יהיה גיל הפרישה – הגיל הקבוע לגביו, בהתאם לחודש לידתו, בחלק א׳ בתוספת;
-- ext:[ral:55] | (2) לגבי אישה שנולדה עד חודש דצמבר 1969, יהיה גיל הפרישה – הגיל הקבוע לגביה, בהתאם לחודש לידתה, בחלק ב׳ בתוספת;
-- ext:[ral:186] | חודש הלידה גיל הזכאות (בשנים)
-- ext:[ral:187] | עד מרס 1939 65
-- ext:[ral:188] | אפריל עד אוגוסט 1939 65 ו־4 חודשים
-- ext:[ral:189] | ספטמבר 1939 עד אפריל 1940 65 ו־8 חודשים
-- ext:[ral:190] | מאי עד דצמבר 1940 66
-- ext:[ral:191] | ינואר עד אוגוסט 1941 66 ו־4 חודשים
-- ext:[ral:192] | ספטמבר 1941 עד אפריל 1942 66 ו־8 חודשים
-- ext:[ral:200] | מאי 1947 עד דצמבר 1959 62
-- ext:[ral:201] | ינואר 1960 עד דצמבר 1960 62 ו־4 חודשים
-- ext:[ral:202] | ינואר 1961 עד דצמבר 1961 62 ו־8 חודשים
-- ext:[ral:203] | ינואר 1962 עד דצמבר 1962 63
-- ext:[ral:204] | ינואר 1963 עד דצמבר 1963 63 ו־3 חודשים
-- ext:[ral:205] | ינואר 1964 עד דצמבר 1964 63 ו־6 חודשים
-- ext:[ral:206] | ינואר 1965 עד דצמבר 1965 63 ו־9 חודשים
-- ext:[ral:207] | ינואר 1966 עד דצמבר 1966 64
-- ext:[ral:208] | ינואר 1967 עד דצמבר 1967 64 ו־3 חודשים
-- ext:[ral:209] | ינואר 1968 עד דצמבר 1968 64 ו־6 חודשים
-- ext:[ral:210] | ינואר 1969 עד דצמבר 1969 64 ו־9 חודשים

@ref the Retirement Age Law, Part B of the Schedule, lines 199-211 — no row for a woman born before May 1947 (needs a source)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Part B of the Schedule to the Retirement Age Law, as deposited, has no row for a woman born before May 1947` MEANS
    REFUSE "Part B of the Schedule to the Retirement Age Law, as deposited, has no row for a woman born before May 1947"

-- A birth month as a single count: twelve times the year plus the month less one.
@ref the Retirement Age Law, ss 3, 6 and the Schedule
GIVEN p IS A `A person, for the Retirement Age Law`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month count of the birth of` p MEANS
    `the month count of calendar month` (p's `calendar month of birth`) `of` (p's `calendar year of birth`)

-- s 6(1) and Part A: a man born up to April 1942, by birth month (65 years, then 4 months more each stage). s 3: 67 for a man born later.
@ref the Retirement Age Law, ss 3, 6(1), Part A (lines 42, 54, 187-192)
GIVEN p IS A `A person, for the Retirement Age Law`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the retirement age of a man, in months, born as` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the month count of the birth of` p AT MOST `the month count of calendar month` 3 `of` 1939 THEN 65 TIMES 12
        IF `the month count of the birth of` p AT MOST `the month count of calendar month` 8 `of` 1939 THEN 65 TIMES 12 PLUS 4
        IF `the month count of the birth of` p AT MOST `the month count of calendar month` 4 `of` 1940 THEN 65 TIMES 12 PLUS 8
        IF `the month count of the birth of` p AT MOST `the month count of calendar month` 12 `of` 1940 THEN 66 TIMES 12
        IF `the month count of the birth of` p AT MOST `the month count of calendar month` 8 `of` 1941 THEN 66 TIMES 12 PLUS 4
        IF `the month count of the birth of` p AT MOST `the month count of calendar month` 4 `of` 1942 THEN 66 TIMES 12 PLUS 8
        OTHERWISE 67 TIMES 12

-- s 6(2) and Part B: a woman born up to December 1969, by birth month (from May 1947). s 3: 65 for a woman born later.
@ref the Retirement Age Law, ss 3, 6(2), Part B (lines 42, 55, 200-210)
GIVEN p IS A `A person, for the Retirement Age Law`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the retirement age of a woman, in months, born as` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the month count of the birth of` p LESS THAN `the month count of calendar month` 5 `of` 1947 THEN `Part B of the Schedule to the Retirement Age Law, as deposited, has no row for a woman born before May 1947`
        IF `the month count of the birth of` p AT MOST `the month count of calendar month` 12 `of` 1959 THEN 62 TIMES 12
        IF p's `calendar year of birth` EQUALS 1960 THEN 62 TIMES 12 PLUS 4
        IF p's `calendar year of birth` EQUALS 1961 THEN 62 TIMES 12 PLUS 8
        IF p's `calendar year of birth` EQUALS 1962 THEN 63 TIMES 12
        IF p's `calendar year of birth` EQUALS 1963 THEN 63 TIMES 12 PLUS 3
        IF p's `calendar year of birth` EQUALS 1964 THEN 63 TIMES 12 PLUS 6
        IF p's `calendar year of birth` EQUALS 1965 THEN 63 TIMES 12 PLUS 9
        IF p's `calendar year of birth` EQUALS 1966 THEN 64 TIMES 12
        IF p's `calendar year of birth` EQUALS 1967 THEN 64 TIMES 12 PLUS 3
        IF p's `calendar year of birth` EQUALS 1968 THEN 64 TIMES 12 PLUS 6
        IF p's `calendar year of birth` EQUALS 1969 THEN 64 TIMES 12 PLUS 9
        OTHERWISE 65 TIMES 12

@export The retirement age under the Retirement Age Law, 5764-2004 (ss 3 and 6 and the Schedule), in months, of a person by sex and calendar month of birth: a man 65 years to 67 (Part A for those born up to April 1942, then 67), a woman 62 years to 65 (Part B for those born from May 1947 to December 1969, then 65); declines for a woman born before May 1947, whose row Part B, as deposited, lacks
@ref the Retirement Age Law, ss 3, 6, the Schedule
GIVEN p IS A `A person, for the Retirement Age Law`
          @desc sex, and the calendar year and month of birth
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the retirement age, in months, of` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `sex`
    WHEN `a man`   THEN `the retirement age of a man, in months, born as` p
    WHEN `a woman` THEN `the retirement age of a woman, in months, born as` p

-- The calendar month (as a month count) in which the person reaches the retirement age: the month of birth plus the age in months.
@ref the Retirement Age Law, s 3
GIVEN p IS A `A person, for the Retirement Age Law`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month count of the month in which the retirement age is reached by` p MEANS
    `the month count of the birth of` p PLUS `the retirement age, in months, of` p

-- "Has reached the retirement age" in or before a tax year, as Income Tax Ordinance s 37 and others read it (row IL-08, fork F20: in or before the tax year): the age
-- is reached in a calendar month not after December of that year.
@export Whether a person has reached the retirement age of the Retirement Age Law, 5764-2004, in or before a given tax year (the age is reached in a calendar month not after December of that year), as Income Tax Ordinance s 1 "retirement age" and s 37 use it; declines for a woman born before May 1947
@ref the Retirement Age Law, ss 3, 6; ITO s 1 (line 115), s 37
GIVEN p IS A `A person, for the Retirement Age Law`
          @desc sex, and the calendar year and month of birth
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
          @desc the tax year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person` p `has reached the retirement age in or before tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    `the month count of the month in which the retirement age is reached by` p AT MOST `the month count of calendar month` 12 `of` `the tax year`
